{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit","id":263317,"title":"So killing a spirit...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-22T19:04:55-07:00","id":263317,"title":"So killing a spirit...","content":"Effect on the physical world? Say if I kill a deer spirit does a deer just die?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T19:07:05-07:00","id":263330,"title":"","content":"No effect, unless the spirit was regularly influencing something in the physical world, in which case it would obviously stop doing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T19:13:35-07:00","id":263333,"title":"","content":"Ah I've been readin a lot of w20 lately. In te umbra if you kill a tree spirit the tree died","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T19:29:55-07:00","id":263342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=263333#post263333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah I've been readin a lot of w20 lately. In te umbra if you kill a tree spirit the tree died</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe if the said tree was claimed by the spirit but judging on that statement alone, the nWoD's Shadow tends to be less direct than that other than perhaps a locus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T02:30:17-07:00","id":263547,"title":"","content":"Think of it this way: Spirit gets whacked? it's influences cease to exist. If a Jaggling created a whole forest, from nothing, one tree at a time, with something akin to Plant Growth? it all dies off. Not instantly, but as a result of a malady. Maybe even simply attracts the kind of spirits that would benefit with the destruction of this forest, as there isn't a guardian on it anymore. Cue in human agents. If a lesser spirit continuously used Strengthen to assure it's reflection(s) would keep existing, then said reflection will not enjoy this protection any longer, for ill or good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T02:47:57-07:00","id":263558,"title":"","content":"Of course, anything that was <i>competing</i> with the slain spirit to influence (and Influence) the world is now unopposed.<br /> <br /> A deer-spirit might have been fighting off a wolf-spirit, for example, and now the ecology of the forest is thrown out of whack by a sudden explosion of wolves. Or maybe that deer-spirit was helping defend against a monstrous spirit of industry that now threatens to poison the entire forest.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it was just helping that specific deer with Influence 1: Strengthen, and without that help the deer is weaker. It might even die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-23-2014, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T05:08:31-07:00","id":263630,"title":"","content":"I've read couple a weeks ago much on Shadow Realm of WoD, so I can't point out were I found those ( mainly <b>WtF</b> or <b>Bookf of Spirits</b> I read ), but I remember that when killing animal or tree that spring the &quot;shadow&quot; ( non-intelligent, large &quot;prop&quot; of Shadow Realm - basically Rank 0, &quot;sleeping&quot; spirit ) in to consciousnesses by the shock of destruction, and the spirit can awaken by this. It works with objects too - destroy the hammer that generated a &quot;spiritual shadow&quot; of it, and the &quot;shadow&quot; will become free spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T05:24:32-07:00","id":263658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=263547#post263547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think of it this way: Spirit gets whacked? it's influences cease to exist. If a Jaggling created a whole forest, from nothing, one tree at a time, with something akin to Plant Growth? it all dies off. Not instantly, but as a result of a malady. Maybe even simply attracts the kind of spirits that would benefit with the destruction of this forest, as there isn't a guardian on it anymore. Cue in human agents. If a lesser spirit continuously used Strengthen to assure it's reflection(s) would keep existing, then said reflection will not enjoy this protection any longer, for ill or good.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really. Would a forest die only because the forester who kept it vanishes? Does plants wither just because the plant their seeds come from get torn up? The spirit that created the forest just planted and nourished it, but the forest isn't kept alive by the spirit. It's kept alive by the nourishment in the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T05:32:47-07:00","id":263663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=263658#post263658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not really. Would a forest die only because the forester who kept it vanishes? Does plants wither just because the plant their seeds come from get torn up? The spirit that created the forest just planted and nourished it, but the forest isn't kept alive by the spirit. It's kept alive by the nourishment in the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true.<br /> <br /> However, much like the deer spirit in MugaSofer's example, if the forest spirit was using Influence 1: Strengthen on the forest and that was the only thing keeping it from being deforested/burning/destroyed/whatever, then it would start to die.<br /> <br /> Basically, the answer to the OP's question is &quot;All sorts of things <i>could</i> happen when you kill a spirit.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T15:28:00-07:00","id":264168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=263658#post263658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not really. Would a forest die only because the forester who kept it vanishes? Does plants wither just because the plant their seeds come from get torn up? The spirit that created the forest just planted and nourished it, but the forest isn't kept alive by the spirit. It's kept alive by the nourishment in the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>The parasites that would take root on the forest, the spirits that would feed on it's destruction would take root. The nourishment are stolen before they feed the trees, etc, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Actually destroying a spirit is a significant feat. It should bear recognizable consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 09-23-2014, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T02:38:19-07:00","id":264466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=264168#post264168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The parasites that would take root on the forest, the spirits that would feed on it's destruction would take root. The nourishment are stolen before they feed the trees, etc, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Actually destroying a spirit is a significant feat. It should bear recognizable consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree, it would mean the forest is no longer tended, and that is all. <br /> It'd force the forest to fend for itself, which sure would make it more likely that diseases or parasites would gain in strength, but it's not like those things are symptoms of lack-of-spirit. And I think trees are fully capable of feeding themselves, and not needing spirits to do it for them. <br /> <br /> Yeah. It requires a Sacred Hunt, or use a weaponised Bane. It's complicated, but there are tons and tons of spirits, and if one gets destroyed, others will quickly swoop in and start feeding of that delicious essence that isn't eaten by the now-deceased spirit.<br /> <br /> That's my take on it at least. -- Spirits aren't a necessary part of the world, it'll get duller and slower without the influx of Essence and Influences from the Shadow, but it'll work just fine. This isn't Exalted, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T19:33:24-07:00","id":265089,"title":"","content":"Do we know if the hisil has been vastly changed with 2nd ed beyond the God machine updates?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T20:12:27-07:00","id":265125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=265089#post265089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if the hisil has been vastly changed with 2nd ed beyond the God machine updates?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So far no, but we have to wait until they released the book or they post a blog about it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T20:12:46-07:00","id":265126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=265089#post265089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if the hisil has been vastly changed with 2nd ed beyond the God machine updates?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave has noted that Werewolf 2e's presentation of the Shadow will have different emphases than previous takes on the Hisil, though that was at the tail end of a lead-up about how the three or four preceding takes all emphasized different things as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T04:13:15-07:00","id":265307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=265089#post265089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if the hisil has been vastly changed with 2nd ed beyond the God machine updates?</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting thing about the <i>hisil</i> is that different people often have wildly different takes on it despite reading the same source material. As such I expect some people to read Dave's new write-up for it and think it's changed vastly, and others to think it hasn't changed at all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I still really want to do a Shadow book that's just all about the <i>hisil</i>, Shadow-phenomena, spirit politics, etc etc. Not like the Book of Spirits, but something that really focuses on detailing the Shadow and adding lots of depth and game hooks to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T07:27:24-07:00","id":265445,"title":"","content":"To the question - no, nothing happens to the physical deer, except the end of any Influence-based effects that the spirit might have been creating.Without anything feeding on the deer's resonance, it will probably attract a new Rank 0 spirit within a day or two.<br /> <br /> As for the Hisil in second edition...<br /> <br /> * I describe the inside of the Gauntlet. In 1e you stood in one world for the time it took to cross, then crossed. Now, you vanish from one world, hang inside the Gauntlet for a few Turns and then appear on the other side. Sometimes, you see things in there.<br /> <br /> * We've given Helios a purpose and motivation other than just &quot;Luna's twin brother,&quot; which doesn't alter how Helions act toward werewolves but reveals much about the Hisil's &quot;physics&quot;<br /> <br /> * A lot of attention is placed on describing what the Shadow looks, feels, and tastes like - it's a sensory experience, especially for an Uratha.<br /> <br /> * Werewolve's Essence-senses are explicitly perceived as their sense of smell/taste. You don't *see* dormant spirits, you taste them in the not-air.<br /> <br /> * One of the example spirits is a big-box retailer; they act like corpulent slum-lords of the Shadow, enslaving the lesser spirits linked to the goods and consumers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T08:01:45-07:00","id":265473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=265445#post265445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * We've given Helios a purpose and motivation other than just &quot;Luna's twin brother,&quot; which doesn't alter how Helions act toward werewolves but reveals much about the Hisil's &quot;physics&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably my personal favourite bit of the new write-up as it adds a lot to the Shadow in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T08:17:22-07:00","id":265481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=265445#post265445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the question - no, nothing happens to the physical deer, except the end of any Influence-based effects that the spirit might have been creating.Without anything feeding on the deer's resonance, it will probably attract a new Rank 0 spirit within a day or two.<br /> <br /> As for the Hisil in second edition...<br /> <br /> * I describe the inside of the Gauntlet. In 1e you stood in one world for the time it took to cross, then crossed. Now, you vanish from one world, hang inside the Gauntlet for a few Turns and then appear on the other side. Sometimes, you see things in there.<br /> <br /> * We've given Helios a purpose and motivation other than just &quot;Luna's twin brother,&quot; which doesn't alter how Helions act toward werewolves but reveals much about the Hisil's &quot;physics&quot;<br /> <br /> * A lot of attention is placed on describing what the Shadow looks, feels, and tastes like - it's a sensory experience, especially for an Uratha.<br /> <br /> * Werewolve's Essence-senses are explicitly perceived as their sense of smell/taste. You don't *see* dormant spirits, you taste them in the not-air.<br /> <br /> * One of the example spirits is a big-box retailer; they act like corpulent slum-lords of the Shadow, enslaving the lesser spirits linked to the goods and consumers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The two main things I like are the attention to the sensory experience of the Shadow, which as someone who likes to build atmosphere for in the real world makes me giddy, and the idea of Helios contributing a lot to the Hisil. I'm insanely curious about this now.<br /> <br /> But I love every inch of these ideas.<br /> <br /> God, I'm just so exited for Werewolf all over again-and this was the game that brought me in.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Can you walk on the wall/in the wound/less poetically, the Gauntlet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-25-2014, 11