Wall-Mart would look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 09-25-2014, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T18:16:37-07:00","id":265839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=265806#post265806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: also what would you think the spirit of Wall-Mart would look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I made a Wall-Mart Jaggling once, it breed smaller greed spirits that sucked the life out of other local, smaller business. They resembled dog-sized coppery green ticks. It was called Maw-Mart. It's ban left it defenseless against someone holding a receipt of an item the Wall-Mart sold, from another business, at a better price than what was on it's shelves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T03:55:02-07:00","id":266076,"title":"","content":"I dunno how Dave B might have the spirit of Wal-Mart look, but were I to do the spirit of a big supermarket retailer, the two things that spring to mind are:<br /> <br /> 1) The spirit of a specific store. A vast monstrosity of steel and concrete, cables and lights, that clatters and skitters along the ceiling of the superstore's Shadow impression. To a large extent, the whole building is an extension of it, like a spider's web within which it can sense the presence of prey and its spirit-vassals. Think an immense, possibly-arachnid building-spirit-thing that bubbles and drips from strange, organic tumours of greed, hunger and other emotions, with too many limbs and too many eyes - some of which may look like immense human eyes, others may have the appearance of CCTV cameras or television screens, warped and twisted extrusions from the spirit's bulk. It's big, the size of an elephant, yet somehow hurries along the ceiling with disturbing speed, diving down on threads of thick cabling and ropy, muscly sinew to confront intruders or snatch up prey.<br /> <br /> 2) The spirit at the heart of the whole business. The interior of the headquarters building is a hive - a complex pattern of cells and corridors that don't really match the building's real layout. Drone-spirits of work and fear rush from place to place, or squat in their little cells and stare across the Gauntlet at the office worker they are bonded to. Greedy things lurch along, lapping with their slithery tongues at the Essence that seethes across into the Shadow from the constant efforts of the human workforce. Go deep enough into the hive and you'll find the heart, the queen bee, an array of whirling limbs, spheres of flesh and machinery, threads of gristle reaching between its parts as they dance in the patterns of a great, vile orrery. It has so many faces, flipping from the face of a mascot or a logo, the face of a CEO or an advertisement's actor; talking to it is disorientating as its personas constantly dance and switch, and its voice is an entire choir of chanting throats in unison. Its tendrils plunge deep into the building around it, oozing roots of spirit-meat. Each limb, each spinning sphere, is bound with long stretches of papers and silks, marked with sigils of First Tongue and of greed, of corporate organisation and of profit reports. It can, temporarily, force its shape down into a humanoid form, a grey-skinned and featureless person in a suit, but this facade cannot be contained for long; it will soon rupture and burst out again to reveal the alien, inhuman force behind the human front.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T04:04:03-07:00","id":266079,"title":"","content":"<b>Acrozatarim</b>, so cool description. Would look on what have <b>Dave B</b> to say on topic of this &quot;physicals&quot; of spirits.<br /> <br /> To return to the main topic - what consequence could killing Wall-Mart stores spirit? What would be for killing Wall - Queen - Mart in headquarters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T17:13:10-07:00","id":266518,"title":"","content":"Hi there, new member here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I wanted to pop in this topic as I find the whole thing where Spirits and them being removed through whatever means affects the general resonant vicinity they are linked to. I pretty much agree with the idea that if a Spirit of a Resonant location is taken down, likely whatever Spirits were close by and eyeing the place up likely move in, if the Resonance itself is changed then that likely brings a whole different bunch of Spirits about... The Forest Spirit being removed from Essence bleed when it's Resonant Forest is replaced with a Wal-Mart likely means a whole bunch of Store Spirits gather around, or y'know... whatever...<br /> Now to answer the last post, I'd say taking down the Wal-Mart Spirit likely will have an effect on the store... It likely loses customers, bad things happen... Eventually it shuts down. Depending on what Spirits are close by it'd change to suit them... Perhaps smaller Forest Spirits staved off by the defeated Spirit come in and take over the place, leaving the deserted store overgrown with vines and weeds... Thats my take on it at least <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Now I wanna be involved in a Werewolf game that's similar to Princess Mononoke with all this Forest Spirit talk <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T04:50:03-07:00","id":267312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=266076#post266076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno how Dave B might have the spirit of Wal-Mart look, but were I to do the spirit of a big supermarket retailer, the two things that spring to mind are:<br /> <br /> 1) The spirit of a specific store. A vast monstrosity of steel and concrete, cables and lights, that clatters and skitters along the ceiling of the superstore's Shadow impression. To a large extent, the whole building is an extension of it, like a spider's web within which it can sense the presence of prey and its spirit-vassals. Think an immense, possibly-arachnid building-spirit-thing that bubbles and drips from strange, organic tumours of greed, hunger and other emotions, with too many limbs and too many eyes - some of which may look like immense human eyes, others may have the appearance of CCTV cameras or television screens, warped and twisted extrusions from the spirit's bulk. It's big, the size of an elephant, yet somehow hurries along the ceiling with disturbing speed, diving down on threads of thick cabling and ropy, muscly sinew to confront intruders or snatch up prey.<br /> <br /> 2) The spirit at the heart of the whole business. The interior of the headquarters building is a hive - a complex pattern of cells and corridors that don't really match the building's real layout. Drone-spirits of work and fear rush from place to place, or squat in their little cells and stare across the Gauntlet at the office worker they are bonded to. Greedy things lurch along, lapping with their slithery tongues at the Essence that seethes across into the Shadow from the constant efforts of the human workforce. Go deep enough into the hive and you'll find the heart, the queen bee, an array of whirling limbs, spheres of flesh and machinery, threads of gristle reaching between its parts as they dance in the patterns of a great, vile orrery. It has so many faces, flipping from the face of a mascot or a logo, the face of a CEO or an advertisement's actor; talking to it is disorientating as its personas constantly dance and switch, and its voice is an entire choir of chanting throats in unison. Its tendrils plunge deep into the building around it, oozing roots of spirit-meat. Each limb, each spinning sphere, is bound with long stretches of papers and silks, marked with sigils of First Tongue and of greed, of corporate organisation and of profit reports. It can, temporarily, force its shape down into a humanoid form, a grey-skinned and featureless person in a suit, but this facade cannot be contained for long; it will soon rupture and burst out again to reveal the alien, inhuman force behind the human front.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. This is awesome, and I simply have to use this in my game.<br /> <br /> I think I speak for the entire forum when I say that this is awesome, and You are awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T11:01:48-07:00","id":268355,"title":"","content":"I was of the understanding that if you killed the spirit of a deer the deer that &quot;birthed&quot; it would sort of wither and die. Am I wrong in this assumption?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T11:31:01-07:00","id":268399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=268355#post268355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was of the understanding that if you killed the spirit of a deer the deer that &quot;birthed&quot; it would sort of wither and die. Am I wrong in this assumption?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you are wrong. The Shadow and the Flesh are related, but not on a 1:1 basis. Things in one can affect the other, but it's not a perfect mirror. A deer in the Flesh is as hearty and deer-like as any other deer. While it does Deer Things, some Deer Essence will appear in the Shadow in that area. Some Spirits will be attracted to this Essence, and come to nom on it. If the spirits are strong enough to do so, they will attempt to protect the Deer by Strengthening it, or by messing with things that might try to harm the deer.<br /> <br /> When those spirits are killed, the deer merely loses its supernatural protectors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T14:40:26-07:00","id":268551,"title":"","content":"To add to that though, Spirits have their own Influences and are linked to something that has a specific Resonance... So whilst the Shadow and Flesh aren't related at a 1:1 basis, doing something like killing the flesh deer would mess the Spirits over if the Resonance they took Essence from was the deer itself. The weakened Spirits may then be replaced by other Spirits biding their time in the area, like Death or Slaughter spirits... It all depends on how the deer dies and what Spirits gain Essence from how the area has been affected...<br /> <br /> The main point is an area Resonant with something attracts the spirits that can gain Essence from such an area. When the Resonance is removed or changed to no longer feed those spirits, new ones will come in or the Spirits themselves may change by feeding off each other to survive to become something else entirely... At least thats how I see it. YMMV and I haven't played W:tF for some time now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T00:12:06-07:00","id":270644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/263317-so-killing-a-spirit?p=265588#post265588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jeez what kind of things would you even see in the gauntlet? Trapped uratha that botched a roll (or is that only apocalypse?)? Maybe azlu spinning away...</div> </div> </div> </div> Summoners for Mage mentioned things that exist in the Gauntlet, so it's been established, if not elaborated on too much. <br /> <br /> Hmm, now I'm wondering if spirits going from the hisil to the material world have to stay in the gauntlet a bit too, if yes than the ecologies of the gauntlet and the hisil would be connected, if not, then the things in the gauntlet ought to be alien to the hisil and vice versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}